vsm1.9:55.2:
Of course, there are other synonyms too for all “beings,” such as all “folks,” all “souls,” etc.;
still it is for clarity’s sake that “The mind-deliverance of loving-kindness is practiced with unspecified
pervasion in five ways” is said and that only these five are mentioned.

vsm1.9:71.1:
Fire, poison and weapons do not affect him: they do not affect, do not enter into, the body of one who abides in loving-kindness,
like the fire in the case of the lay woman devotee Uttarā (see XII.34 and Dhp-a III 310), like the poison in the case
of the Saṃyutta reciter the Elder Cūḷa-Siva, like the knife in the case of the novice Saṅkicca (see Dhp-a II 249);
